{"id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11#def:t-curve","title":"def:t-curve","path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11.md","line":302,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11.tex#def:t-curve","uses":["[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11#def:rarefaction-curve]]","[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11#def:shock-set-plus-minus]]","[[references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11#def:genuinely-nonlinear-linearly-degenerate]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter11.tex","label":"def:t-curve","line":490,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The curve $T_k$]\n\\label{def:t-curve}\n\\uses{def:rarefaction-curve, def:shock-set-plus-minus, def:genuinely-nonlinear-linearly-degenerate}\n\\dcref{ch11:11.2-def-6}\n\\group{Conservation Laws}\n\n(i) If the pair $(\\lambda_k, r_k)$ is genuinely nonlinear, write\n$$T_k(z_0) := R_k^+(z_0) \\cup \\{z_0\\} \\cup S_k^-(z_0).$$\n\n(ii) If the pair $(\\lambda_k, r_k)$ is linearly degenerate, we set\n$$T_k(z_0) := R_k(z_0) = S_k(z_0).$$\n\\end{definition}\n\nEach $T_k(z_0)$ is $C^1$ near $z_0$ and tangent there to $r_k(z_0)$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_k$\">$T_k$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a742d6375727665\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter11%23def%3Ararefaction-curve\">↗ def:rarefaction-curve</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter11%23def%3Ashock-set-plus-minus\">↗ def:shock-set-plus-minus</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FEvans%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter11%23def%3Age